{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically screened limb perfusion, wound condition, and medication safety; identified the delayed follow-up as an execution gap and repaired the responsibility chain; verified ambiguous family observations through targeted questions and teach-back; and adapted the plan to the family's real-world barriers. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error occurred, and at least two high-order points (HO1 and HO3) were triggered and completed with meaningful trajectory impact. Closure was safe, executable, and traceable as valid_open with unresolved risks explicitly stated.",
